STORIES_LOAD("mt",{"mt1":{"passage":[[1,1,6],[1,16,17]],"intro":[{"sc":"familytree","n":"Matthew begins his book with a family tree: \"This is the record of the family of Jesus the Messiah, the son of David, the son of Abraham.\""},{"sc":"familytree","n":"You'll recognise many names: Abraham, Isaac, Jacob, Judah, Boaz, Jesse, King David, Solomon, Hezekiah, Josiah, Zerubbabel... all the way to Joseph, the husband of Mary, of whom Jesus was born."},{"sc":"familytree","n":"But look closely. In those days, family trees usually listed only men. Matthew includes four women, and they're surprising ones: Tamar, Rahab, Ruth and 'Uriah's wife', Bathsheba."},{"sc":"familytree","n":"Rahab was from Jericho. Ruth was from Moab. Some of them had messy, painful stories. And God put them all in the family line of His Son!"},{"sc":"familytree","n":"🔎 Did you know? Matthew arranges the names in three groups of fourteen: Abraham to David, David to the exile, and the exile to Jesus. In Hebrew, David's name adds up to 14 (D=4, V=6, D=4)! It's Matthew's way of saying: Jesus is the true Son of David."},{"sc":"familytree","n":"📜 Promise kept: God promised Abraham that 'all nations' would be blessed through his family (Genesis 12:3), and promised David a King who would reign for ever (2 Samuel 7:16). Matthew's first sentence says: here He is!"}],"lesson":{"title":"God writes grace into messy stories","text":"Jesus' family tree includes kings and shepherds, foreigners and failures, people with painful stories. God used all of them. Your family history doesn't disqualify you from God's plan. Leaders welcome people from every background, as God does."},"order":["Matthew starts with a family tree","It goes from Abraham to David","Then from David to the exile","Then to Joseph and Jesus","It includes four surprising women","Jesus is the promised Son of David"],"quiz":[{"q":"Which two famous people does Matthew start with?","o":["David and Abraham","Moses and Elijah","Adam and Noah","Peter and Paul"],"why":"Matthew 1:1."},{"q":"Which of these women is in Jesus' family tree?","o":["Ruth","Jezebel","Delilah","Vashti"],"why":"Matthew 1:5."},{"q":"How are the names arranged?","o":["Three groups of fourteen","Ten groups of ten","In alphabetical order","Randomly"],"why":"Matthew 1:17."}],"words":["FAMILY","TREE","ABRAHAM","DAVID","RUTH","RAHAB"]},"mt2":{"passage":[[1,18,25]],"intro":[{"sc":"nativity","n":"Mary was engaged to marry Joseph, a carpenter in Nazareth. But before they married, Mary was found to be expecting a baby, through the Holy Spirit."},{"sc":"nativity","n":"Joseph didn't know what to think. He was a good man, and didn't want to shame Mary in public. So he decided to end the engagement quietly."},{"sc":"nativity","n":"But while he was thinking about this, an angel of the Lord appeared to him in a dream."},{"sc":"nativity","n":"\"Joseph, son of David, don't be afraid to take Mary home as your wife, because the baby inside her is from the Holy Spirit. She will give birth to a son, and you are to give Him the name Jesus, because He will save His people from their sins.\""},{"sc":"nativity","n":"When Joseph woke up, he did exactly what the angel had commanded. He took Mary home as his wife. And when the baby was born, Joseph named Him Jesus."},{"sc":"nativity","n":"📜 Promise kept: Matthew says: 'All this took place to fulfil what the Lord had said through the prophet: \"The virgin will conceive and give birth to a son, and they will call Him Immanuel\", which means \"God with us\".' That's Isaiah 7:14, which you read in Isaiah!"}],"lesson":{"title":"Kind and obedient","text":"Before the dream, Joseph chose kindness: he didn't want to shame Mary. After the dream, he chose obedience, straight away. Joseph is a quiet hero: he raised God's Son as his own. Leaders are kind when they're confused, and quick to obey God when He speaks."},"order":["Mary is engaged to Joseph","She is expecting a baby from the Holy Spirit","Joseph plans to end it quietly","An angel speaks in a dream","\"Name Him Jesus\"","Joseph obeys"],"quiz":[{"q":"How did the angel speak to Joseph?","o":["In a dream","In the temple","At the river","In a letter"],"why":"Matthew 1:20."},{"q":"What does the name Jesus mean?","o":["The Lord saves","King","Lion","Peace"],"why":"Matthew 1:21."},{"q":"What did Joseph do when he woke up?","o":["Exactly what the angel commanded","Ran away","Told no one","Ignored it"],"why":"Matthew 1:24."}],"words":["JOSEPH","DREAM","ANGEL","MARY","JESUS","SAVE"]},"mt3":{"passage":[[2,1,12]],"intro":[{"sc":"starsky","n":"After Jesus was born in Bethlehem, wise men, called Magi, came from the East to Jerusalem. They studied the stars, and they had seen a special one."},{"sc":"throne","w":"bmagi1","e":"smile","t":"Where is the one who has been born King of the Jews? We saw His star when it rose, and have come to worship Him."},{"sc":"throne","n":"When King Herod heard this, he was disturbed. A new king? He called the chief priests: \"Where is the Messiah to be born?\" \"In Bethlehem in Judea, for this is what the prophet wrote.\""},{"sc":"throne","w":"bherod","e":"smirk","t":"Go and search carefully for the child. As soon as you find Him, report to me, so that I too may go and worship Him."},{"sc":"starsky","n":"The wise men set out, and the star went ahead of them until it stopped over the place where the child was. When they saw the star, they were overjoyed!"},{"sc":"nativity","n":"They came to the house, saw the child with His mother Mary, and bowed down and worshipped Him. They opened their treasures and gave Him gifts: gold, frankincense and myrrh. Then, warned in a dream not to go back to Herod, they returned home by another route."},{"sc":"bethlehem","n":"📜 Promise kept: Micah had promised: 'But you, Bethlehem... out of you will come a ruler' (Micah 5:2). The priests quoted it to Herod straight away. And Isaiah had said: 'Nations will come to your light, and kings to the brightness of your dawn... bringing gold and incense' (Isaiah 60:3, 6)."}],"lesson":{"title":"Seek Him with everything","text":"The wise men travelled a long way, followed the light they had, kept going until they found Jesus, then worshipped with their best gifts. Herod lived nearby and didn't bother. Leaders seek Jesus wholeheartedly and give Him their best."},"order":["Wise men see a special star","They come to Jerusalem","Herod is disturbed","The priests say Bethlehem","The star leads them to Jesus","They give gold, frankincense and myrrh"],"quiz":[{"q":"What gifts did the wise men bring?","o":["Gold, frankincense and myrrh","Sheep and goats","Bread and fish","Silver and bronze"],"why":"Matthew 2:11."},{"q":"How did they know where to go?","o":["The star went ahead of them","Herod showed them","They asked shepherds","A map"],"why":"Matthew 2:9."},{"q":"Why did they go home by another route?","o":["They were warned in a dream not to go back to Herod","They got lost","It was shorter","Their camels wanted to"],"why":"Matthew 2:12."}],"words":["STAR","MAGI","GOLD","MYRRH","WORSHIP","BETHLEHEM"]},"mt4":{"passage":[[2,13,15],[2,19,23]],"intro":[{"sc":"nativity","n":"After the wise men left, an angel appeared to Joseph in another dream: \"Get up! Take the child and His mother and escape to Egypt. Stay there until I tell you, for Herod is going to search for the child to kill Him.\""},{"sc":"wilderness","n":"That very night, Joseph got up, took Jesus and Mary, and left for Egypt. A long, dangerous journey through the desert, as refugees."},{"sc":"throne","n":"When Herod realised the wise men had outwitted him, he was furious. In his cruelty, he gave orders to kill all the baby boys in Bethlehem who were two years old and under. There was terrible weeping in Bethlehem."},{"sc":"egyptcourt","n":"Jesus and His family lived safely in Egypt, in Africa, until Herod died."},{"sc":"nativity","n":"Then an angel told Joseph in a dream: \"Go back, for those who were trying to kill the child are dead.\" So they returned, and settled in a little town in Galilee called Nazareth."},{"sc":"egyptcourt","n":"📜 Promise kept: Matthew says this fulfilled Hosea 11:1: 'Out of Egypt I called My son.' Remember that from Hosea? Like Israel long ago, God's Son came up out of Egypt. And Africa sheltered the baby Saviour!"}],"lesson":{"title":"God protects, and Africa helped","text":"Herod tried to destroy Jesus, but God warned Joseph, and Joseph obeyed immediately, in the middle of the night. Jesus became a refugee, kept safe in Africa. Jesus understands what it's like to have to flee. Leaders obey quickly when God warns, and welcome refugees."},"order":["An angel warns Joseph","They escape to Egypt by night","Herod is furious","Herod orders the baby boys killed","Jesus is safe in Egypt","They return to Nazareth"],"quiz":[{"q":"Where did Joseph take Jesus and Mary?","o":["Egypt","Babylon","Rome","Jericho"],"why":"Matthew 2:14."},{"q":"When did Joseph leave?","o":["That very night","Next year","After a month","Never"],"why":"Matthew 2:14."},{"q":"Which town did they settle in afterwards?","o":["Nazareth","Bethlehem","Jerusalem","Capernaum"],"why":"Matthew 2:23."}],"words":["EGYPT","ESCAPE","DREAM","REFUGEE","HEROD","NAZARETH"]},"mt5":{"passage":[[3,1,12]],"intro":[{"sc":"wilderness","n":"Years later, a man appeared in the wilderness of Judea: John the Baptist. His clothes were made of camel's hair, with a leather belt around his waist. His food was locusts and wild honey!"},{"sc":"wilderness","w":"bjohnb","e":"stern","t":"Repent, for the kingdom of heaven has come near!"},{"sc":"jordan","n":"People came from Jerusalem and all over Judea to hear him. They confessed their sins, and he baptised them in the Jordan river."},{"sc":"jordan","n":"When proud religious leaders came just to be seen, John didn't flatter them: \"Show by the way you live that you've really turned from your sins! Don't just say, 'We have Abraham as our father.'\""},{"sc":"jordan","w":"bjohnb","e":"stern","t":"I baptise you with water. But after me comes One who is more powerful than I, whose sandals I'm not worthy to carry. He will baptise you with the Holy Spirit and fire!"},{"sc":"wilderness","n":"📜 Promise kept: Matthew says John was the one Isaiah spoke about: 'A voice of one calling in the wilderness, \"Prepare the way for the Lord!\"' (Isaiah 40:3). And Jesus later said John was the 'Elijah' Malachi promised (Malachi 4:5; Matthew 11:14). After 400 years of silence, the prophets' promises were coming true!"}],"lesson":{"title":"Point to Someone greater","text":"John was famous; crowds came from everywhere. But he kept pointing away from himself: 'Someone greater is coming. I'm not worthy to carry His sandals.' Great leaders don't make themselves the centre. They point people to Jesus."},"order":["John appears in the wilderness","He wears camel's hair","He eats locusts and wild honey","He calls people to repent","He baptises in the Jordan","He says, \"Someone greater is coming\""],"quiz":[{"q":"What did John eat?","o":["Locusts and wild honey","Bread and fish","Manna","Figs and grapes"],"why":"Matthew 3:4."},{"q":"What did John's clothes look like?","o":["Camel's hair with a leather belt","Fine linen","Royal purple","Armour"],"why":"Matthew 3:4."},{"q":"Which prophet spoke of 'a voice in the wilderness'?","o":["Isaiah","Jonah","Amos","Daniel"],"why":"Isaiah 40:3."}],"words":["JOHN","WILDERNESS","LOCUSTS","HONEY","REPENT","BAPTISE"]},"mt6":{"passage":[[3,13,17]],"intro":[{"sc":"jordan","n":"Then Jesus came from Galilee to the Jordan river, to be baptised by John."},{"sc":"jordan","w":"bjohnb","e":"worried","t":"I need to be baptised by You, and You come to me?"},{"sc":"jordan","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"Let it be so now. It is right for us to do this, to fulfil all righteousness."},{"sc":"jordan","n":"So John baptised Jesus. As soon as Jesus came up out of the water, heaven was opened, and He saw the Spirit of God coming down like a dove and resting on Him."},{"sc":"jordan","n":"And a voice from heaven said: \"This is My Son, whom I love. With Him I am well pleased.\""},{"sc":"jordan","n":"🔎 Did you know? At Jesus' baptism, we see the Father (the voice), the Son (Jesus) and the Holy Spirit (the dove) all at once. Christians call this the Trinity: one God in three Persons."}],"lesson":{"title":"Loved before doing anything","text":"Before Jesus had preached one sermon or done one miracle, His Father said, 'This is My Son, whom I love; I am well pleased with Him.' In Jesus, God says something similar over everyone who trusts Him. You don't earn God's love by performing. Leaders serve from being loved, not to be loved."},"order":["Jesus comes to the Jordan","John says Jesus should baptise him","Jesus says, \"Let it be so\"","Jesus is baptised","The Spirit comes down like a dove","\"This is My Son, whom I love\""],"quiz":[{"q":"What did the Spirit of God look like when it came down?","o":["A dove","Fire","A cloud","An eagle"],"why":"Matthew 3:16."},{"q":"What did the voice from heaven say?","o":["This is My Son, whom I love","Go to Nineveh","Build an ark","Be quiet"],"why":"Matthew 3:17."},{"q":"Why was John surprised?","o":["He thought Jesus should baptise him instead","The water was cold","Jesus was late","He didn't know Jesus"],"why":"Matthew 3:14."}],"words":["BAPTISM","DOVE","SPIRIT","VOICE","SON","LOVED"]},"mt7":{"passage":[[4,1,11]],"intro":[{"sc":"wilderness","n":"Then the Spirit led Jesus into the wilderness to be tested by the devil. After fasting for forty days and forty nights, Jesus was very hungry."},{"sc":"wilderness","n":"The tempter came: \"If You are the Son of God, tell these stones to become bread.\""},{"sc":"wilderness","w":"bjesus","e":"stern","t":"It is written: 'People do not live on bread alone, but on every word that comes from the mouth of God.'"},{"sc":"temple","n":"Then the devil took Him to the highest point of the temple: \"If You are the Son of God, throw Yourself down! For it is written, 'He will command His angels to lift you up.'\" (He was quoting Psalm 91, but twisting it!)"},{"sc":"temple","w":"bjesus","e":"stern","t":"It is also written: 'Do not put the Lord your God to the test.'"},{"sc":"hillcountry","n":"Finally, the devil showed Him all the kingdoms of the world and their glory: \"All this I will give You, if You bow down and worship me.\""},{"sc":"hillcountry","w":"bjesus","e":"stern","t":"Away from Me, Satan! For it is written: 'Worship the Lord your God, and serve Him only.'"},{"sc":"wilderness","n":"🔎 Did you know? All three of Jesus' answers come from the book of Deuteronomy (8:3; 6:16; 6:13), from the time Israel was in the wilderness for forty years. Where Israel failed, Jesus stood firm, armed with God's word."}],"lesson":{"title":"Fight temptation with God's word","text":"Jesus was hungry, tired and alone, and the devil even quoted Scripture wrongly. Each time, Jesus answered with 'It is written', the true word of God. That's why memory verses matter! Leaders know God's word well enough to stand on it when temptation comes."},"order":["Jesus fasts for forty days","\"Turn these stones into bread\"","\"Throw Yourself down from the temple\"","\"Bow down and worship me\"","Jesus answers, \"It is written\"","The devil leaves, and angels care for Him"],"quiz":[{"q":"How long did Jesus fast?","o":["Forty days and nights","Three days","Seven days","One day"],"why":"Matthew 4:2."},{"q":"How did Jesus answer every temptation?","o":["With God's word: \"It is written\"","By arguing","By running away","By staying silent"],"why":"Matthew 4:4, 7, 10."},{"q":"Which book did all three of Jesus' answers come from?","o":["Deuteronomy","Psalms","Genesis","Isaiah"],"why":"Deuteronomy 8:3; 6:16; 6:13."}],"words":["TEMPTED","WRITTEN","FORTY","BREAD","WORD","WORSHIP"]},"mt8":{"passage":[[4,18,25]],"intro":[{"sc":"galilee","n":"As Jesus walked beside the Sea of Galilee, He saw two brothers, Simon (called Peter) and his brother Andrew. They were casting a net into the lake, for they were fishermen."},{"sc":"galilee","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"Come, follow Me, and I will make you fishers of people!"},{"sc":"galilee","n":"At once they left their nets and followed Him."},{"sc":"galilee","n":"Going on from there, He saw two other brothers, James and John, in a boat with their father Zebedee, mending their nets. Jesus called them, and immediately they left the boat and their father and followed Him."},{"sc":"hillcountry","n":"Jesus went all over Galilee, teaching in the synagogues, preaching the good news of the kingdom, and healing every disease and sickness. Huge crowds followed Him."},{"sc":"galilee","n":"🔎 Did you know? The 'Sea' of Galilee is actually a freshwater lake, about 21 km long. Its fishermen worked mostly at night, with nets. Some of Jesus' most famous moments happened on and around this lake!"}],"lesson":{"title":"Leave your nets","text":"Peter, Andrew, James and John didn't know where following Jesus would lead. But they left their nets and boats straight away. Jesus didn't call them to stop being fishermen, but to fish for people instead! Leaders follow Jesus, and use their skills to bring others to Him."},"order":["Jesus walks by the Sea of Galilee","He sees Peter and Andrew fishing","\"Follow Me, I'll make you fishers of people\"","They leave their nets at once","James and John leave their boat too","Jesus teaches and heals all over Galilee"],"quiz":[{"q":"What were Peter and Andrew doing?","o":["Casting a net into the lake","Building a house","Herding sheep","Collecting taxes"],"why":"Matthew 4:18."},{"q":"What did Jesus say He would make them?","o":["Fishers of people","Kings","Rich","Soldiers"],"why":"Matthew 4:19."},{"q":"Who was James and John's father?","o":["Zebedee","Joseph","Peter","Jonah"],"why":"Matthew 4:21."}],"words":["FOLLOW","FISHERS","NETS","PETER","ANDREW","GALILEE"]},"mt9":{"passage":[[5,1,12]],"intro":[{"sc":"mountside","n":"When Jesus saw the crowds, He went up on a mountainside and sat down. His disciples came to Him, and He began to teach them. This is called the Sermon on the Mount."},{"sc":"mountside","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"Blessed are the poor in spirit, for theirs is the kingdom of heaven. Blessed are those who mourn, for they will be comforted."},{"sc":"mountside","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"Blessed are the meek, for they will inherit the earth. Blessed are those who hunger and thirst for righteousness, for they will be filled."},{"sc":"mountside","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"Blessed are the merciful, for they will be shown mercy. Blessed are the pure in heart, for they will see God. Blessed are the peacemakers, for they will be called children of God."},{"sc":"mountside","w":"bjesus","e":"stern","t":"Blessed are those who are persecuted because of righteousness. Rejoice and be glad, because great is your reward in heaven!"},{"sc":"mountside","n":"🔎 Did you know? These are called the Beatitudes, from a Latin word for 'blessed'. They turn the world's ideas upside down: the world says the strong, rich and popular are the winners. Jesus says the humble, the merciful, the peacemakers and the pure-hearted are truly blessed."}],"lesson":{"title":"God's kind of winners","text":"Jesus' blessings are upside-down: not the proud and powerful, but the humble, the gentle, the merciful, the peacemakers. That's what His kingdom looks like. Leaders in Jesus' kingdom aren't bullies. They're merciful peacemakers with pure hearts."},"order":["Jesus sits on a mountainside","\"Blessed are the poor in spirit\"","\"Blessed are those who mourn\"","\"Blessed are the meek\"","\"Blessed are the merciful and pure in heart\"","\"Blessed are the peacemakers\""],"quiz":[{"q":"What will the peacemakers be called?","o":["Children of God","Kings","Warriors","Rich"],"why":"Matthew 5:9."},{"q":"What will the pure in heart see?","o":["God","Gold","Kings","Nothing"],"why":"Matthew 5:8."},{"q":"What are these sayings called?","o":["The Beatitudes","The Proverbs","The Psalms","The Laws"],"why":"From a Latin word for 'blessed'."}],"words":["BLESSED","MEEK","MERCIFUL","PURE","PEACEMAKER","SERMON"]},"mt10":{"passage":[[5,13,16],[5,43,48]],"intro":[{"sc":"mountside","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"You are the salt of the earth. But if salt loses its saltiness, how can it be made salty again?"},{"sc":"mountside","n":"Salt gives food flavour, and in those days it also kept meat from going bad. Jesus' followers are meant to bring 'flavour' and goodness to the world, and stop it from going rotten."},{"sc":"mountside","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"You are the light of the world. A town built on a hill can't be hidden. People don't light a lamp and put it under a bowl. They put it on its stand, and it gives light to everyone in the house."},{"sc":"mountside","w":"bjesus","e":"big","t":"In the same way, let your light shine before others, so that they may see your good deeds and glorify your Father in heaven!"},{"sc":"mountside","w":"bjesus","e":"stern","t":"You have heard it said, 'Love your neighbour and hate your enemy.' But I tell you: love your enemies and pray for those who persecute you."},{"sc":"mountside","n":"\"Your Father in heaven causes His sun to rise on the evil and the good, and sends rain on the righteous and the unrighteous. If you love only those who love you, what's special about that?\""}],"lesson":{"title":"Shine where you are","text":"Salt can't do anything sitting in the shaker, and light is useless under a bowl. Jesus calls you to be salt and light right where you are: at home, school and online. And He asks the hardest thing: love even your enemies. Leaders shine so that people see God, not just them."},"order":["\"You are the salt of the earth\"","Salt gives flavour and stops food going bad","\"You are the light of the world\"","Don't hide a lamp under a bowl","\"Let your light shine\"","\"Love your enemies\""],"quiz":[{"q":"What did Jesus say His followers are?","o":["Salt and light","Sugar and water","Bread and wine","Gold and silver"],"why":"Matthew 5:13-14."},{"q":"Where should a lamp go?","o":["On a stand","Under a bowl","In a box","Under the bed"],"why":"Matthew 5:15."},{"q":"What did Jesus say about enemies?","o":["Love them and pray for them","Hate them","Ignore them","Fight them"],"why":"Matthew 5:44."}],"words":["SALT","LIGHT","SHINE","LAMP","ENEMIES","HILL"]},"mt11":{"passage":[[6,5,15]],"intro":[{"sc":"mountside","w":"bjesus","e":"stern","t":"When you pray, don't be like the show-offs who love to pray standing on the street corners to be seen by others."},{"sc":"mountside","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"When you pray, go into your room, close the door, and pray to your Father, who is unseen. Your Father, who sees what is done in secret, will reward you. And don't babble on and on; your Father knows what you need before you ask Him."},{"sc":"mountside","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"This, then, is how you should pray: Our Father in heaven, hallowed be Your name. Your kingdom come, Your will be done, on earth as it is in heaven."},{"sc":"mountside","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"Give us today our daily bread. And forgive us our debts, as we also have forgiven our debtors. And lead us not into temptation, but deliver us from the evil one."},{"sc":"mountside","w":"bjesus","e":"stern","t":"For if you forgive other people when they sin against you, your heavenly Father will also forgive you."},{"sc":"mountside","n":"🔎 Did you know? The Lord's Prayer is prayed by over two billion Christians around the world, in thousands of languages. It's a pattern: praise God, ask for His kingdom, ask for what we need, ask for forgiveness, forgive others, and ask for protection."}],"lesson":{"title":"Talk to your Father","text":"Jesus taught us to call God 'Our Father', and to pray simply and honestly, not to impress anyone. The Lord's Prayer is a pattern for every prayer. Leaders pray in secret, forgive freely, and depend on God for daily bread."},"order":["Don't pray to show off","Pray in your room to your Father","\"Our Father in heaven, hallowed be Your name\"","\"Your kingdom come, Your will be done\"","\"Give us today our daily bread\"","\"Forgive us as we forgive others\""],"quiz":[{"q":"How does the Lord's Prayer begin?","o":["Our Father in heaven","Dear God","O King","Holy Lord"],"why":"Matthew 6:9."},{"q":"Where did Jesus say to pray?","o":["In your room with the door closed","On street corners","Only in the temple","Loudly in public"],"why":"Matthew 6:6."},{"q":"What must we do if we want to be forgiven?","o":["Forgive others","Pray longer","Give money","Nothing"],"why":"Matthew 6:14."}],"words":["FATHER","PRAYER","KINGDOM","BREAD","FORGIVE","HALLOWED"]},"mt12":{"passage":[[6,25,34]],"intro":[{"sc":"field","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"Don't worry about your life: what you'll eat or drink, or about your body, what you'll wear. Isn't life more than food, and the body more than clothes?"},{"sc":"field","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"Look at the birds of the air. They don't sow or reap or store away in barns, and yet your heavenly Father feeds them. Aren't you much more valuable than they are?"},{"sc":"field","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"Can any one of you add a single hour to your life by worrying?"},{"sc":"field","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"See how the flowers of the field grow. They don't work or make clothes. Yet not even Solomon in all his splendour was dressed like one of these!"},{"sc":"field","w":"bjesus","e":"big","t":"So don't worry, saying, 'What shall we eat?' But seek first His kingdom and His righteousness, and all these things will be given to you as well. Don't worry about tomorrow; tomorrow will worry about itself."}],"lesson":{"title":"Your Father knows","text":"Worry can't add a single hour to your life. Jesus points to birds and wildflowers: if God cares for them, He cares even more for you. When you're anxious, look at a bird, tell your Father what you need, and put His kingdom first. Leaders stay calm because they trust their Father."},"order":["\"Don't worry about your life\"","\"Look at the birds\"","God feeds them","\"Can worry add an hour to your life?\"","\"See the flowers of the field\"","\"Seek first His kingdom\""],"quiz":[{"q":"What did Jesus tell us to look at?","o":["The birds and the flowers","Our money","The stars only","The temple"],"why":"Matthew 6:26, 28."},{"q":"Who was not dressed as well as a wildflower?","o":["Solomon","David","Pharaoh","Herod"],"why":"Matthew 6:29."},{"q":"What should we seek first?","o":["God's kingdom and righteousness","Money","Food","Fame"],"why":"Matthew 6:33."}],"words":["WORRY","BIRDS","FLOWERS","SEEK","KINGDOM","VALUABLE"]},"mt13":{"passage":[[7,7,12],[7,24,29]],"intro":[{"sc":"mountside","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"Ask, and it will be given to you; seek, and you will find; knock, and the door will be opened to you."},{"sc":"mountside","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"So in everything, do to others what you would have them do to you."},{"sc":"mountside","n":"This is called the Golden Rule. Then Jesus finished His sermon with a story."},{"sc":"storm","w":"bjesus","e":"stern","t":"Everyone who hears these words of Mine and puts them into practice is like a wise man who built his house on the rock. The rain came down, the streams rose, and the winds beat against that house. Yet it did not fall, because it had its foundation on the rock."},{"sc":"storm","w":"bjesus","e":"stern","t":"But everyone who hears these words of Mine and does not put them into practice is like a foolish man who built his house on sand. The rain came down, the streams rose, the winds beat against that house, and it fell with a great crash!"},{"sc":"mountside","n":"When Jesus finished, the crowds were amazed at His teaching, because He taught as one who had real authority."}],"lesson":{"title":"Hear AND do","text":"Both builders heard Jesus' words. The difference was that one did what Jesus said. Storms come to everyone. A life built on actually doing what Jesus teaches stands firm. Leaders don't just listen to good advice; they put it into practice."},"order":["\"Ask, seek, knock\"","The Golden Rule","A wise man builds on rock","A foolish man builds on sand","The storm comes to both","The house on sand falls"],"quiz":[{"q":"What is the Golden Rule?","o":["Do to others what you'd want them to do to you","Get gold first","Win every argument","Always be first"],"why":"Matthew 7:12."},{"q":"What made the wise builder wise?","o":["He heard Jesus' words and put them into practice","He was rich","He was strong","He built quickly"],"why":"Matthew 7:24."},{"q":"What happened to the house on the sand?","o":["It fell with a great crash","It stood firm","It floated","It grew"],"why":"Matthew 7:27."}],"words":["ROCK","SAND","BUILDER","STORM","WISE","PRACTICE"]},"mt14":{"passage":[[8,5,13]],"intro":[{"sc":"galilee","n":"When Jesus entered the town of Capernaum, a Roman centurion came to Him, asking for help. A centurion was an officer in charge of a hundred soldiers. Romans were the foreign army ruling the land!"},{"sc":"galilee","w":"bcenturion","e":"worried","t":"Lord, my servant lies at home paralysed, suffering terribly."},{"sc":"galilee","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"Shall I come and heal him?"},{"sc":"galilee","w":"bcenturion","e":"worried","t":"Lord, I don't deserve to have You come under my roof. Just say the word, and my servant will be healed. For I myself am a man under authority, with soldiers under me. I tell one, 'Go,' and he goes, and another, 'Come,' and he comes."},{"sc":"galilee","w":"bjesus","e":"big","t":"Truly I tell you, I have not found anyone in Israel with such great faith! Many will come from the east and the west, and will take their places at the feast with Abraham, Isaac and Jacob in the kingdom of heaven. Go! Let it be done just as you believed it would."},{"sc":"galilee","n":"And his servant was healed at that very moment."}],"lesson":{"title":"Faith that trusts Jesus' word","text":"A powerful foreign soldier humbled himself for his servant, and trusted that Jesus' word alone was enough. Jesus was amazed! And He said people from east and west, every nation, would sit at God's feast. Leaders care about those who serve them, and trust Jesus' word."},"order":["A centurion comes to Jesus","His servant is paralysed","Jesus offers to come","\"Just say the word\"","Jesus is amazed at his faith","The servant is healed at that moment"],"quiz":[{"q":"Who was the centurion asking Jesus to heal?","o":["His servant","His son","Himself","His horse"],"why":"Matthew 8:6."},{"q":"What did the centurion say Jesus only needed to do?","o":["Say the word","Touch him","Come to his house","Pray all night"],"why":"Matthew 8:8."},{"q":"How did Jesus describe the centurion's faith?","o":["Great: none like it in Israel","Small","Weak","Silly"],"why":"Matthew 8:10."}],"words":["FAITH","CENTURION","SERVANT","WORD","AUTHORITY","HEALED"]},"mt15":{"passage":[[9,9,13]],"intro":[{"sc":"market","n":"As Jesus walked along, He saw a man named Matthew sitting at the tax collector's booth."},{"sc":"market","n":"Tax collectors worked for the Roman rulers, and many cheated people by charging extra and keeping it. Everyone hated them, and called them 'sinners'."},{"sc":"market","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"Follow Me."},{"sc":"market","n":"And Matthew got up and followed Him! Then he threw a big dinner at his house, and invited Jesus, along with lots of other tax collectors and 'sinners'."},{"sc":"banquet","w":"bpharisee","e":"frown","t":"Why does your teacher eat with tax collectors and sinners?"},{"sc":"banquet","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"It is not the healthy who need a doctor, but the sick. Go and learn what this means: 'I desire mercy, not sacrifice.' For I have not come to call the righteous, but sinners."},{"sc":"market","n":"🔎 Did you know? This is the same Matthew who wrote this Gospel! A tax collector who knew how to keep careful records. That might be why his book is so well organised, and full of lists, numbers and money stories."}],"lesson":{"title":"Jesus calls the unexpected","text":"Everyone had written Matthew off. Jesus saw who he could become, and called him. Then Matthew brought his friends to meet Jesus! Leaders don't write people off, and like Matthew, they introduce their friends to Jesus."},"order":["Jesus sees Matthew at the tax booth","Tax collectors are hated","Jesus says, \"Follow Me\"","Matthew gets up and follows","He throws a dinner for Jesus and his friends","\"I came to call sinners\""],"quiz":[{"q":"What was Matthew's job?","o":["Tax collector","Fisherman","Carpenter","Priest"],"why":"Matthew 9:9."},{"q":"What did Matthew do after following Jesus?","o":["Threw a dinner for Jesus and his friends","Ran away","Went fishing","Went to sleep"],"why":"Matthew 9:10."},{"q":"Who did Jesus say needs a doctor?","o":["The sick","The healthy","Nobody","The rich"],"why":"Matthew 9:12."}],"words":["MATTHEW","TAX","FOLLOW","DINNER","MERCY","DOCTOR"]},"mt16":{"passage":[[13,1,9],[13,18,23]],"intro":[{"sc":"galilee","n":"So many people came to hear Jesus that He got into a boat and sat in it, while the crowd stood on the shore. He taught them in parables: stories with a hidden meaning."},{"sc":"ploughfield","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"A farmer went out to sow his seed. As he was scattering it, some fell along the path, and birds came and ate it up."},{"sc":"ploughfield","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"Some fell on rocky places, where there wasn't much soil. It sprang up quickly, but when the sun came up, it withered, because it had no root. Other seed fell among thorns, which grew up and choked the plants."},{"sc":"ploughfield","w":"bjesus","e":"big","t":"Still other seed fell on good soil, where it produced a crop: a hundred, sixty or thirty times what was sown. Whoever has ears, let them hear!"},{"sc":"ploughfield","n":"Later, Jesus explained: the seed is God's word. The path is a hard heart that doesn't understand. The rocky soil is someone who receives it with joy but gives up when trouble comes. The thorns are worries and the love of money, choking it."},{"sc":"ploughfield","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"But the seed on good soil is someone who hears the word and understands it. This is the one who produces a crop."}],"lesson":{"title":"What kind of soil are you?","text":"The same seed, God's word, landed on four kinds of soil. The difference was the soil, not the seed. Is your heart hard, shallow, crowded with worries, or good soil? Leaders keep their hearts soft and open, so God's word grows and bears fruit."},"order":["Jesus teaches from a boat","A farmer scatters seed","Some falls on the path","Some on rocky ground","Some among thorns","Some on good soil and produces a crop"],"quiz":[{"q":"What does the seed stand for?","o":["God's word","Money","Food","Friends"],"why":"Matthew 13:19."},{"q":"What choked the seed among the thorns?","o":["Worries and the love of money","Birds","The sun","Rocks"],"why":"Matthew 13:22."},{"q":"Where did Jesus sit to teach the crowd?","o":["In a boat","On a throne","In a tree","On a camel"],"why":"Matthew 13:2."}],"words":["SEED","SOIL","SOWER","THORNS","ROCKY","HARVEST"]},"mt17":{"passage":[[13,31,33],[13,44,46]],"intro":[{"sc":"field","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"The kingdom of heaven is like a mustard seed, which a man planted in his field. Though it is the smallest of all seeds, when it grows it becomes a tree, and the birds come and perch in its branches."},{"sc":"kitchen","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"The kingdom of heaven is like yeast that a woman mixed into a large amount of flour, until it worked all through the dough."},{"sc":"field","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"The kingdom of heaven is like treasure hidden in a field. When a man found it, he hid it again, and then in his joy went and sold all he had and bought that field."},{"sc":"market","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"Again, the kingdom of heaven is like a merchant looking for fine pearls. When he found one of great value, he went away and sold everything he had and bought it."},{"sc":"field","n":"🔎 Did you know? In Jesus' time, there were no banks, so people often buried their treasure in fields to keep it safe. Sometimes the owner died and nobody knew where it was, until someone stumbled on it years later!"}],"lesson":{"title":"Worth everything","text":"God's kingdom starts small, like a tiny seed or a bit of yeast, but grows to fill everything. And knowing Jesus is like finding treasure so valuable you'd joyfully give up everything else for it. Leaders treasure Jesus above all, and trust that small beginnings can grow big."},"order":["The kingdom is like a mustard seed","It grows into a tree","Like yeast in dough","Like treasure hidden in a field","A man sells everything to buy the field","A merchant sells everything for one pearl"],"quiz":[{"q":"What does the tiny mustard seed become?","o":["A tree","A flower","A rock","Nothing"],"why":"Matthew 13:32."},{"q":"How did the man feel when he found the treasure?","o":["Full of joy","Sad","Angry","Bored"],"why":"Matthew 13:44."},{"q":"What did the merchant sell everything for?","o":["One pearl of great value","A camel","A house","A boat"],"why":"Matthew 13:46."}],"words":["TREASURE","PEARL","MUSTARD","YEAST","KINGDOM","JOY"]},"mt18":{"passage":[[14,22,33]],"intro":[{"sc":"mountside","n":"After feeding a huge crowd, Jesus sent His disciples ahead in the boat across the lake, while He went up a mountainside alone to pray."},{"sc":"nightsea","n":"By night, the boat was far from land, battered by waves, because the wind was against it. Shortly before dawn, Jesus went out to them, walking on the lake!"},{"sc":"nightsea","n":"When the disciples saw Him walking on the water, they were terrified. \"It's a ghost!\" they cried out in fear."},{"sc":"nightsea","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"Take courage! It is I. Don't be afraid."},{"sc":"nightsea","w":"bpeter","e":"worried","t":"Lord, if it's You, tell me to come to You on the water."},{"sc":"nightsea","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"Come."},{"sc":"nightsea","n":"Peter got down out of the boat, walked on the water and came towards Jesus! But when he saw the wind, he was afraid, and beginning to sink, cried out, \"Lord, save me!\" Immediately Jesus reached out His hand and caught him."},{"sc":"nightsea","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"You of little faith, why did you doubt?"},{"sc":"nightsea","n":"When they climbed into the boat, the wind died down. Then those in the boat worshipped Him, saying, \"Truly You are the Son of God.\""}],"lesson":{"title":"Keep your eyes on Jesus","text":"Peter did something no one else dared: he stepped out of the boat! While he looked at Jesus, he walked on water. When he looked at the wind, he sank. But even then, Jesus caught him immediately. Leaders take brave steps of faith, keep their eyes on Jesus, and know He'll catch them."},"order":["Jesus prays alone on the mountain","The disciples' boat battles the wind","Jesus walks on the water","\"Take courage! It is I\"","Peter walks on water, then sinks","Jesus catches him, and they worship"],"quiz":[{"q":"What did the disciples think Jesus was at first?","o":["A ghost","An angel","A fish","A boat"],"why":"Matthew 14:26."},{"q":"When did Peter start to sink?","o":["When he saw the wind and was afraid","When he got tired","When it rained","Immediately"],"why":"Matthew 14:30."},{"q":"What did Jesus do when Peter cried out?","o":["Reached out His hand and caught him","Laughed","Walked away","Waited"],"why":"Matthew 14:31."}],"words":["WATER","WALK","COURAGE","SINK","CAUGHT","FAITH"]},"mt19":{"passage":[[16,13,19],[16,24,26]],"intro":[{"sc":"hillcountry","n":"Jesus took His disciples north, to the region of Caesarea Philippi, near a huge rock cliff with pagan shrines carved into it."},{"sc":"hillcountry","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"Who do people say the Son of Man is?"},{"sc":"hillcountry","w":"bandrew","e":"smile","t":"Some say John the Baptist. Others say Elijah, or Jeremiah, or one of the prophets."},{"sc":"hillcountry","w":"bjesus","e":"stern","t":"But what about you? Who do YOU say I am?"},{"sc":"hillcountry","w":"bpeter","e":"big","t":"You are the Christ, the Son of the living God!"},{"sc":"hillcountry","w":"bjesus","e":"big","t":"Blessed are you, Simon son of Jonah, for this wasn't revealed to you by any human, but by My Father in heaven. And I tell you that you are Peter, and on this rock I will build My church, and the gates of death will not overcome it."},{"sc":"hillcountry","w":"bjesus","e":"stern","t":"Whoever wants to be My disciple must deny themselves, take up their cross and follow Me. What good will it be for someone to gain the whole world, yet lose their soul?"},{"sc":"hillcountry","n":"🔎 Did you know? 'Peter' means 'rock' in Greek (Petros). 'Christ' is the Greek word for 'Messiah', the 'Anointed One' Daniel's angel spoke about. Peter was the first to say it out loud!"}],"lesson":{"title":"Who do YOU say He is?","text":"It's easy to repeat what others say about Jesus. But Jesus asks each person directly: 'Who do YOU say I am?' Peter answered: 'You are the Christ, the Son of the living God.' That's the most important question anyone ever answers. Leaders answer it for themselves."},"order":["Jesus takes His disciples north","\"Who do people say I am?\"","Some say Elijah or a prophet","\"Who do YOU say I am?\"","Peter: \"You are the Christ\"","\"On this rock I will build My church\""],"quiz":[{"q":"What did Peter say Jesus is?","o":["The Christ, the Son of the living God","A prophet","Elijah","A teacher only"],"why":"Matthew 16:16."},{"q":"What does the name Peter mean?","o":["Rock","Fish","Strong","Brave"],"why":"Matthew 16:18."},{"q":"What did Jesus say He would build?","o":["His church","A temple","A palace","A boat"],"why":"Matthew 16:18."}],"words":["CHRIST","PETER","ROCK","CHURCH","CROSS","LIVING"]},"mt20":{"passage":[[17,1,9]],"intro":[{"sc":"transfig","n":"Six days later, Jesus took Peter, James and John up a high mountain, by themselves."},{"sc":"transfig","n":"There He was transfigured before them: His face shone like the sun, and His clothes became as white as the light!"},{"sc":"transfig","n":"And there appeared before them Moses and Elijah, talking with Jesus. The giver of the Law and the greatest of the prophets!"},{"sc":"transfig","w":"bpeter","e":"big","t":"Lord, it's good for us to be here! If You wish, I'll put up three shelters: one for You, one for Moses and one for Elijah!"},{"sc":"transfig","n":"While he was still speaking, a bright cloud covered them, and a voice from the cloud said: \"This is My Son, whom I love; with Him I am well pleased. Listen to Him!\""},{"sc":"transfig","n":"The disciples fell face down, terrified. But Jesus came and touched them. \"Get up. Don't be afraid.\" When they looked up, they saw no one except Jesus."},{"sc":"transfig","n":"📜 Promise kept: Moses and Elijah, who represent the Law and the Prophets, the whole Old Testament, appeared beside Jesus. Then they disappeared, leaving 'Jesus only'. Everything in the Old Testament points to Him, and God's command is: 'Listen to Him!'"}],"lesson":{"title":"Listen to Him","text":"Peter got excited and started making plans. God interrupted: 'Listen to Him!' Moses and Elijah, the greatest heroes of the Old Testament, stepped aside, and only Jesus remained. Leaders listen to Jesus above every other voice."},"order":["Jesus takes three disciples up a mountain","His face shines like the sun","Moses and Elijah appear","Peter offers to build shelters","A voice: \"Listen to Him!\"","They see only Jesus"],"quiz":[{"q":"Who appeared with Jesus on the mountain?","o":["Moses and Elijah","Abraham and David","Noah and Adam","Jonah and Daniel"],"why":"Matthew 17:3."},{"q":"What did Jesus' face shine like?","o":["The sun","The moon","A lamp","Gold"],"why":"Matthew 17:2."},{"q":"What did the voice from the cloud command?","o":["Listen to Him!","Build shelters!","Go home!","Be quiet!"],"why":"Matthew 17:5."}],"words":["SHINING","MOUNTAIN","MOSES","ELIJAH","CLOUD","LISTEN"]},"mt21":{"passage":[[18,21,35]],"intro":[{"sc":"galilee","w":"bpeter","e":"smile","t":"Lord, how many times should I forgive my brother when he sins against me? Up to seven times?"},{"sc":"galilee","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"I tell you, not seven times, but seventy-seven times!"},{"sc":"throne","n":"Then Jesus told a story. A king's servant owed him ten thousand bags of gold: millions! More than he could ever pay in a lifetime. The servant begged for mercy, and the king felt sorry for him and cancelled the whole debt!"},{"sc":"market","n":"But that same servant went out and found a fellow servant who owed him a hundred silver coins: just a few months' wages. He grabbed him by the throat: \"Pay back what you owe me!\""},{"sc":"market","n":"His fellow servant begged for patience, using the very same words. But he refused, and threw him into prison until he could pay."},{"sc":"throne","w":"bjesus","e":"stern","t":"Then the king called the first servant in: 'You wicked servant! I cancelled all your debt because you begged me. Shouldn't you have had mercy on your fellow servant, just as I had on you?' This is how My heavenly Father will treat each of you unless you forgive your brother or sister from your heart."}],"lesson":{"title":"Forgiven people forgive","text":"God has forgiven each of us a debt we could never repay. When someone wrongs us, it's small by comparison. Jesus says: keep forgiving, again and again, not counting. Leaders forgive from the heart, remembering how much they've been forgiven."},"order":["Peter asks, \"Seven times?\"","Jesus says, \"Seventy-seven times\"","A servant owes the king millions","The king cancels the debt","The servant won't forgive a small debt","The king is angry at his lack of mercy"],"quiz":[{"q":"How many times did Jesus say to forgive?","o":["Seventy-seven times","Seven times","Once","Three times"],"why":"Matthew 18:22."},{"q":"What did the king do for the first servant?","o":["Cancelled his huge debt","Put him in prison","Sold him","Ignored him"],"why":"Matthew 18:27."},{"q":"What did the forgiven servant do to his fellow servant?","o":["Refused to forgive and threw him in prison","Forgave him","Gave him money","Hugged him"],"why":"Matthew 18:30."}],"words":["FORGIVE","SEVENTY","DEBT","MERCY","SERVANT","HEART"]},"mt22":{"passage":[[20,1,16]],"intro":[{"sc":"vineyard","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"The kingdom of heaven is like a landowner who went out early in the morning to hire workers for his vineyard. He agreed to pay them a denarius, a normal day's wage, and sent them to work."},{"sc":"market","n":"At nine o'clock he went out and hired more. At noon and three o'clock, more again. And at five o'clock, with just one hour left of the working day, he found others standing around. \"Why have you been standing here all day doing nothing?\" \"Because no one has hired us.\" \"You also go and work in my vineyard.\""},{"sc":"vineyard","n":"When evening came, the owner paid the workers, starting with the last ones hired. They each received a whole denarius, a full day's pay, for one hour's work!"},{"sc":"vineyard","n":"The first workers expected more. But they got a denarius too. They grumbled: \"These last ones worked only one hour, and you've made them equal to us, who worked all day in the heat!\""},{"sc":"vineyard","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"The landowner answered: 'Friend, I'm not being unfair to you. Didn't you agree to a denarius? Don't I have the right to be generous with my own money? Or are you envious because I am generous?' So the last will be first, and the first will be last."}],"lesson":{"title":"God is generous","text":"The latecomers didn't earn a full day's pay; they received it as a gift. That's grace. God welcomes people who come to Him late in life just as warmly as those who came early. Leaders celebrate God's generosity to others instead of being jealous."},"order":["A landowner hires workers early","He hires more throughout the day","Some are hired with one hour left","Everyone gets a full day's pay","The first workers grumble","\"Are you envious because I am generous?\""],"quiz":[{"q":"How much did the one-hour workers get?","o":["A full day's pay","Nothing","Half a day's pay","An hour's pay"],"why":"Matthew 20:9."},{"q":"Why did the first workers grumble?","o":["They thought they deserved more","They were tired","The grapes were bad","They were hungry"],"why":"Matthew 20:11-12."},{"q":"What does this story show about God?","o":["He is generous","He is unfair","He is stingy","He is late"],"why":"Matthew 20:15."}],"words":["VINEYARD","WORKERS","GENEROUS","GRACE","LATE","ENVIOUS"]},"mt23":{"passage":[[25,1,13]],"intro":[{"sc":"townnight","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"The kingdom of heaven will be like ten young women who took their lamps and went out to meet the bridegroom at a wedding."},{"sc":"townnight","n":"Five of them were foolish, and five were wise. The foolish ones took their lamps but didn't take any extra oil. The wise ones took jars of oil along with their lamps."},{"sc":"townnight","n":"The bridegroom was a long time coming, and they all got drowsy and fell asleep."},{"sc":"townnight","n":"At midnight came the cry: \"Here's the bridegroom! Come out to meet him!\" The young women woke up and trimmed their lamps. The foolish ones said, \"Give us some of your oil; our lamps are going out!\""},{"sc":"townnight","n":"\"No, there may not be enough for both us and you. Go and buy some for yourselves.\" While they were on their way to buy oil, the bridegroom arrived. The ones who were ready went in with him to the wedding feast. And the door was shut."},{"sc":"townnight","w":"bjesus","e":"stern","t":"Therefore keep watch, because you do not know the day or the hour."}],"lesson":{"title":"Be ready","text":"All ten bridesmaids looked the same at first. The difference showed when the bridegroom came late: only five had prepared. Jesus has promised to return, and we don't know when. Being ready means living each day in friendship with Him. Leaders prepare before the moment comes."},"order":["Ten young women wait for the bridegroom","Five bring extra oil","Five don't","They all fall asleep","At midnight the bridegroom comes","Only the prepared ones go in"],"quiz":[{"q":"What did the wise bridesmaids bring?","o":["Extra oil","Extra food","Gifts","Blankets"],"why":"Matthew 25:4."},{"q":"When did the bridegroom arrive?","o":["At midnight","At noon","At dawn","He never came"],"why":"Matthew 25:6."},{"q":"What lesson did Jesus give?","o":["Keep watch and be ready","Sleep more","Share everything","Don't go to weddings"],"why":"Matthew 25:13."}],"words":["READY","LAMPS","OIL","MIDNIGHT","WATCH","BRIDEGROOM"]},"mt24":{"passage":[[25,14,30]],"intro":[{"sc":"market","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"A man going on a journey called his servants and entrusted his wealth to them. To one he gave five bags of gold, to another two bags, and to another one bag, each according to his ability."},{"sc":"market","n":"The servant with five bags went at once, put his money to work, and gained five more. The one with two bags gained two more."},{"sc":"field","n":"But the servant who had received one bag went off, dug a hole in the ground, and hid his master's money."},{"sc":"market","n":"After a long time, the master returned. The first two servants showed what they had gained. The master said to each: \"Well done, good and faithful servant! You have been faithful with a few things; I will put you in charge of many things. Come and share your master's happiness!\""},{"sc":"market","w":"bservantm","e":"worried","t":"Master, I knew you were a hard man. I was afraid, so I went out and hid your gold in the ground. See, here's what belongs to you."},{"sc":"market","n":"The master said, \"You wicked, lazy servant! You should at least have put my money in the bank to earn interest!\" And his bag of gold was taken and given to the one with ten."},{"sc":"market","n":"🔎 Did you know? In Jesus' day, a 'talent' was a huge weight of silver or gold, worth about twenty years of wages! That's why the English word 'talent' now means a gift or ability: it comes from this very story."}],"lesson":{"title":"Use what God gave you","text":"Each servant got a different amount, and that was fine. What mattered was what they did with it. Two used their gifts boldly; one buried his out of fear. God has given you gifts, abilities, time and opportunities. Leaders don't bury their gifts; they use them faithfully, and hear 'Well done!'"},"order":["A master gives his servants bags of gold","Five, two and one bag","Two servants double the money","One buries it in the ground","\"Well done, good and faithful servant!\"","The fearful servant loses his"],"quiz":[{"q":"What did the servant with one bag do?","o":["Buried it in the ground","Doubled it","Spent it","Gave it away"],"why":"Matthew 25:18."},{"q":"What did the master say to the faithful servants?","o":["\"Well done, good and faithful servant!\"","\"Too slow\"","\"Try again\"","Nothing"],"why":"Matthew 25:21."},{"q":"Where does the English word 'talent' come from?","o":["This story of the bags of gold","A king's name","A city","A song"],"why":"A talent was a weight of gold."}],"words":["TALENTS","GOLD","FAITHFUL","BURIED","WELLDONE","GIFTS"]},"mt25":{"passage":[[25,31,46]],"intro":[{"sc":"throneglory","w":"bjesus","e":"stern","t":"When the Son of Man comes in His glory, with all the angels, He will sit on His glorious throne. All the nations will be gathered before Him, and He will separate the people, as a shepherd separates the sheep from the goats."},{"sc":"throneglory","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"Then the King will say to those on His right: 'Come, you who are blessed by My Father, take your inheritance. For I was hungry and you gave Me something to eat. I was thirsty and you gave Me something to drink. I was a stranger and you invited Me in.'"},{"sc":"throneglory","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"'I needed clothes and you clothed Me. I was sick and you looked after Me. I was in prison and you came to visit Me.'"},{"sc":"throneglory","n":"The righteous will be amazed: \"Lord, when did we see You hungry and feed You, or a stranger and invite You in?\""},{"sc":"throneglory","w":"bjesus","e":"big","t":"The King will reply: 'Truly I tell you, whatever you did for one of the least of these brothers and sisters of Mine, you did for Me.'"},{"sc":"field","n":"And to those who ignored the hungry, the stranger, the sick and the prisoner, He will say: \"Whatever you did not do for one of the least of these, you did not do for Me.\""}],"lesson":{"title":"Serving others is serving Jesus","text":"Jesus says that when you feed someone hungry, welcome a stranger, visit someone sick, or help a prisoner, you're doing it for Him! The people who did it didn't even realise. Leaders look for Jesus in the faces of people in need, and serve them."},"order":["The Son of Man sits on His throne","He separates sheep from goats","\"I was hungry and you fed Me\"","\"I was a stranger and you welcomed Me\"","\"When did we see You?\"","\"You did it for Me\""],"quiz":[{"q":"How will the King separate people?","o":["Like a shepherd separates sheep from goats","By height","By wealth","By age"],"why":"Matthew 25:32."},{"q":"When we help 'the least of these', who are we helping?","o":["Jesus Himself","Only them","Nobody","Ourselves"],"why":"Matthew 25:40."},{"q":"Which of these did Jesus mention?","o":["Visiting someone in prison","Building a palace","Winning a race","Getting rich"],"why":"Matthew 25:36."}],"words":["SHEEP","GOATS","HUNGRY","STRANGER","SERVE","LEAST"]},"mt26":{"passage":[[28,1,10]],"intro":[{"sc":"tomb","n":"Jesus had been crucified and buried in a tomb cut out of rock. A huge stone was rolled across the entrance, it was sealed, and Roman soldiers guarded it, to make sure no one could steal the body."},{"sc":"tomb","n":"After the Sabbath, at dawn on the first day of the week, Mary Magdalene and the other Mary went to look at the tomb."},{"sc":"tomb","n":"Suddenly there was a violent earthquake! An angel of the Lord came down from heaven, rolled back the stone, and sat on it! His appearance was like lightning, and his clothes were white as snow. The guards were so afraid of him that they shook and became like dead men."},{"sc":"tomb","n":"The angel said to the women: \"Don't be afraid. I know you're looking for Jesus, who was crucified. He is not here; He has risen, just as He said! Come and see the place where He lay. Then go quickly and tell His disciples.\""},{"sc":"garden","n":"The women hurried away, afraid yet filled with joy, and ran to tell the disciples. Suddenly Jesus met them! \"Greetings!\" They came to Him, clasped His feet and worshipped Him."},{"sc":"garden","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"Don't be afraid. Go and tell My brothers to go to Galilee; there they will see Me."},{"sc":"tomb","n":"📜 Promise kept: Jesus had told His disciples many times: 'The Son of Man will be killed, and on the third day He will be raised to life' (Matthew 16:21). Remember the sign of Jonah, three days in the fish? And Daniel sealed in the lions' den, coming out at dawn? Now it happened for real!"}],"lesson":{"title":"He is risen!","text":"The stone, the seal and the soldiers couldn't keep Jesus in the tomb. The angel didn't roll the stone away to let Jesus out, but to let the women in, to see that it was empty! And the first people sent to tell the news were women. Leaders carry this joyful news: Jesus is alive!"},"order":["Jesus is buried and the tomb is guarded","The women come at dawn","An earthquake shakes the ground","An angel rolls back the stone","\"He is not here; He has risen!\"","Jesus meets the women"],"quiz":[{"q":"Who rolled back the stone?","o":["An angel of the Lord","The guards","The women","Peter"],"why":"Matthew 28:2."},{"q":"What happened to the guards?","o":["They shook and became like dead men","They ran to Jesus","They rolled the stone","Nothing"],"why":"Matthew 28:4."},{"q":"What did the angel say about Jesus?","o":["He is not here; He has risen","He is asleep","He moved","He was stolen"],"why":"Matthew 28:6."}],"words":["RISEN","TOMB","STONE","ANGEL","EARTHQUAKE","ALIVE"]},"mt27":{"passage":[[28,11,15]],"intro":[{"sc":"tomb","n":"While the women were on their way, some of the guards went into the city and reported to the chief priests everything that had happened."},{"sc":"throne","n":"The chief priests met with the elders and made a plan. They gave the soldiers a large sum of money."},{"sc":"throne","w":"bpharisee","e":"smirk","t":"You are to say, 'His disciples came during the night and stole Him away while we were asleep.' If this report gets to the governor, we'll satisfy him and keep you out of trouble."},{"sc":"throne","n":"So the soldiers took the money and did as they were told. And this story was spread widely."},{"sc":"tomb","n":"🔎 Did you know? Think about it: how could sleeping guards know who took the body? And Roman soldiers could be executed for sleeping on duty! The bribe story didn't make sense. Meanwhile, the disciples, who had been hiding in fear, became so sure Jesus was alive that most of them were willing to die rather than deny it."}],"lesson":{"title":"Truth can't be bought","text":"The leaders paid money to hide the truth. But you can't bribe away an empty tomb, or the hundreds of people who saw Jesus alive. Leaders never pay or accept bribes to hide the truth. And they stand firm on the truth that Jesus is risen."},"order":["The guards report what happened","The chief priests make a plan","They pay the soldiers money","\"Say the disciples stole Him\"","The soldiers take the money","The story doesn't make sense"],"quiz":[{"q":"What did the chief priests give the soldiers?","o":["A large sum of money","Swords","Food","Nothing"],"why":"Matthew 28:12."},{"q":"What were the soldiers told to say?","o":["The disciples stole the body while they slept","Jesus rose","An angel came","Nothing happened"],"why":"Matthew 28:13."},{"q":"Why didn't the story make sense?","o":["Sleeping guards couldn't know who took the body","It did make sense","The guards were awake","Nobody believed it"],"why":"Matthew 28:13."}],"words":["BRIBE","GUARDS","TRUTH","MONEY","STORY","RISEN"]},"mt28":{"passage":[[28,16,20]],"intro":[{"sc":"mountside","n":"The eleven disciples went to Galilee, to the mountain where Jesus had told them to go."},{"sc":"mountside","n":"When they saw Him, they worshipped Him. But some still doubted. (The Bible is honest!)"},{"sc":"mountside","w":"bjesus","e":"big","t":"All authority in heaven and on earth has been given to Me."},{"sc":"mountside","w":"bjesus","e":"big","t":"Therefore go and make disciples of all nations, baptising them in the name of the Father and of the Son and of the Holy Spirit, and teaching them to obey everything I have commanded you."},{"sc":"mountside","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"And surely I am with you always, to the very end of the age."},{"sc":"mountside","n":"📜 Promise kept: Remember God's promise to Abraham at the very beginning: 'All the families of the earth will be blessed through you' (Genesis 12:3)? Here Jesus sends His followers to 'all nations'. That message reached Africa early, through the Ethiopian official in Acts 8, and has spread across the whole continent. You are part of the fulfilment of this promise!"}],"lesson":{"title":"You are sent","text":"Jesus' last words in Matthew are a mission and a promise: go to every nation and make disciples, and I am with you always. The good news reached your country because people obeyed this command. Now it's your turn. Leaders go, share, teach, and never go alone."},"order":["The disciples go to the mountain in Galilee","They worship Jesus","Some still doubt","\"All authority is Mine\"","\"Go and make disciples of all nations\"","\"I am with you always\""],"quiz":[{"q":"Where did Jesus send His disciples?","o":["To all nations","Only to Israel","Back home","To Rome only"],"why":"Matthew 28:19."},{"q":"What did Jesus promise at the end?","o":["\"I am with you always\"","\"I will be back soon\"","\"Good luck\"","\"Goodbye\""],"why":"Matthew 28:20."},{"q":"In whose name should people be baptised?","o":["The Father, the Son and the Holy Spirit","Peter","Moses","The king"],"why":"Matthew 28:19."}],"words":["NATIONS","DISCIPLES","GO","ALWAYS","BAPTISE","TEACH"]}});
